course: dictionary
lesson: 7883
title: Ranch and the words around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A ranch is a very large farm, mostly in the USA, Canada or Australia, where cattle, horses or sheep are raised. You can often work out a word by the place it is in. Look for clues: where it happens, who is there, and what they do.
explain: «People cut and burn parts of the Amazon for farms and ranches, and because trees help make the Amazon's rain, when trees go, less rain falls, soil washes away and animals lose homes.» The sentence puts ranches next to farms, so they are both places where people use land. Cutting trees for them causes problems for the whole forest.
explain: Ranch can also be a verb: to ranch means to run a ranch or raise animals on one. Be careful, because «ranch dressing» is a creamy salad dressing, not a farm at all. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, try each meaning in the sentence and see which one fits.
fact: A ranch is a very large farm where cattle, horses or sheep are raised.
fact: Ranches are most often found in the USA, Canada and Australia.
fact: Ranches cover huge areas of grassland.
fact: «Ranch» can be a verb: to ranch means to run a ranch or raise animals on one.
fact: «Ranch dressing» is a creamy salad dressing, and a «ranch house» is a long, one-storey house.
exercise: What is a ranch? | A tiny shop that sells cattle | A kind of rain that falls in the desert | *A very large farm where cattle, horses or sheep are raised | A forest with no trees in it
exercise: In «People cut and burn parts of the Amazon for farms and ranches», what do farms and ranches have in common? | *They both need land, so people clear forest for them | They both are found in cities | They are both tiny | They both sell salad dressing
exercise: «A ranch has 40 horses and 25 cows.» How many animals are on the ranch altogether? | 75 | *65 | 15 | 55
test: As a verb, what does ranch mean? | To ride a bike very fast | *To run a ranch or raise animals on one | To cut down trees for a city | To sell creamy salad dressing
test: Which phrase names a creamy salad dressing? | *Ranch dressing | Ranch house | On the ranch | Cattle ranch
exam: Why does the Amazon sentence say that clearing trees for ranches is harmful? | Trees are only useful for making paper | *Trees help make the Amazon's rain, so when they go, less rain falls and soil washes away | Ranches need forests to grow their cattle | Trees make ranches taller and stronger
